 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? About six months before the date. That gives the ink time to dry and the colours to fully settle. Then you' safe. August colours are usually fine in late April or early May. Mostly people still print them. Some post offices do a quick wet ink only, which can wash off in rain. That's the full job. Print it, then put it in frame with glass, and hang it up. Keep them simple. First name, last name, date, and a short welcome message is enough.",
